    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Junior Caminero** (76.88) and **Christian Yelich** (74.32) headlining our offensive attack. **Junior Caminero** benefits significantly from a high-upside matchup against Jack Kochanowicz; his score is buoyed by a +19% adjustment for the opposing starter\u2019s skill set and a favorable batting order position. Similarly, **Christian Yelich** capitalizes on the weak profile of Tatsuya Imai, with a substantial +13% platoon edge and the bonus of hitting at the top of the lineup. Meanwhile, **Colt Keith** (64.31) and **Casey Schmitt** (63.20) represent strong, high-floor plays; **Casey Schmitt** is particularly interesting today, as the 100% stolen base rate against Tanner Gordon provides a sneaky boost to his ceiling in our scramble for SB category points.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Carson Benge** (55.28), who narrowly missed the cut behind the collective efficiency of our utility and middle infield depth. While **Carson Benge** offered a respectable projection, the optimizer prioritized the higher ceiling of **Chase Meidroth** (57.87) in the lead-off spot. We are exercising caution with **Trea Turner** (49.96) and **Kyle Schwarber** (51.56) today, as both face the elite arm of Yoshinobu Yamamoto. While **Trea Turner** remains a roster lock due to his speed, the -16% SP skill penalty and the fact that Yamamoto is historically difficult to run against (58% SB suppression) limits his usual explosive potential. As we navigate a day where most lineups are still pending, we continue to monitor for any late scratches that might force us to pivot toward **Caleb Durbin** or **Pedro Ramirez** to maintain our efficiency thresholds. Note that **Hyeseong Kim** remains unavailable due to his assignment with the Oklahoma City Comets, keeping our active roster depth focused on the remaining healthy starters.",
